.TH man 3 "27 March 2025" "1.0" "_printf man page"
.SH NAME
_printf \- Prints into format string
.SH SYNOPSIS 
.BI _printf [FORMAT, ARGUMENTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
_printf is a custom implementation of the Standard .C printf function. It formats and prints data to standard output according to a format string.
Supported format speccifiers include:
.TP %c Prints a single char.
.TP %s Prints a string.
.TP %i Prints an integer
.TP %u Prints an unsigned integer
.TP %o Prints an unsigned octal integer
.TP %x Prints an integer in lowercase hexadecimal
.TP %X Prints an integer in uppercase hexadecimal
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
%c - Prints a single char
.TP
%s - Prints a string
.TP
%i - Prints an integer
.TP
%u - Prints an unsigned integer
.TP
%o - Prints an unsigned octal integer
.TP
%x - Prints hexadecimal in lowercase
.TP
%X - Prints a hexadecimal in uppercase
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP 
int handle_char(va_list args) - Handles the %c format specifier
.TP 
int handle_string(va_list args) - Handles the %s format specifier
.TP 
int handle_percent(va_list args) - Handles the %% format specifier
.TP 
int handle_int(va_list args) - Handles the &d and &i format specifier
.TP 
int handle_unsigned(va_list args) - Handles the %u format specifier
.TP
int handle_binary(va_list args) - Handles the %b format specifier
.TP
int handle_octal(va_list args) - Handles the %o format specifier
.TP
int handle_hex_lower(va_list args) - Handles the %x format specifier
.TP
int handle_hex_upper(va_list args) - Handles the %X format specifier
.TP
int print_number(va_list args) - Prints a signed integer
.TP
int print_binary(unsigned int num) - Prints the binary representation of an unsigned integer
.TP
int print_unsigned_base(int num, int base, int uppercase) - Prints an unsigned integer on its respective base(e.g., decimal, hexadecimal, octal)
.SH RETURN 
Returns -1 if 
.I format is NULL
.SH EXAMPLES
_printf("Hello, %s\\n", "world");
.RS
Output :
.I Hello, World!
.SH SEE ALSO
printf(1)
.SH BUGS
No known bugs.
